        {
          "category": "summary",
          "text": "An update for gnutls is now available for Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.6 Extended Update Support.\n\nRed Hat Product Security has rated this update as having a security impact of Moderate. A Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE link(s) in the References section.",
          "title": "Topic"
        },
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "The gnutls packages provide the GNU Transport Layer Security (GnuTLS) library, which implements cryptographic algorithms and protocols such as SSL, TLS, and DTLS.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* gnutls: GnuTLS: Denial of Service via excessive resource consumption during certificate verification (CVE-2025-14831)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
